A||N||7||shawnster84||Banging noise in front end||||5||
Z||000000||shawnster84||09-25-2001||06:04 PM||||I just replaced the rack and the inner and outer tie rod ends because the car was making a banging noise in the front pass side whenever a went over a little dip or just about anything in the road..I replaced the upper and lower ball joints, sway bar bushings, shocks about 100 miles ago..what gives??? would anybody know why it is still doing this?? I cant figure out where it is coming from because everything under there is new and tight..oh I do need to get it aligned but I don't think that would be the problem..Thanks!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||09-25-2001||06:08 PM||||Let the kids out of the front trunk!<BR>Speaking of that, is anything loose in there???<BR>Drive it up on ramps and see if the radiator mount is solid, or if you can wiggle anything else...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||shawnster84||09-25-2001||06:24 PM||||I'll have to check..but it sure sounds like its coming from the wheel..could bad control arm bushings cause this? Oh..I replaced the wheel bearings too and no luck..||||reg||1
Z||000003||jelly2m8||09-25-2001||06:36 PM||||It might be a bad bushing in the passangers side of the steering rack. Jack the front of the car up and support it with stands, turn the steering wheel to the right ( pass. side). Get underneath, and grab the end of the steering rack where the inner tie rod is screwed fast to, dont be scared to squeeze the bellows boot. Shake the end of the rack up and down, front to back, shake it hard, you wont break nothing. If you feel any significant amount of free play, the bushing is worn out.<P> If you find this, contact Rodney, he can set you up with the bushing for a small fee which will fix up the loose rack. The rack will have to come out, and be disassembled to replace this.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierohoho||09-25-2001||06:58 PM||||I had a similar problem with my '85 a while back, it turned out the top shock mount had broken loose.<P>Easy to check but a little harder to fix, had to have a friend weld it.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Patrick's Dad||09-25-2001||10:23 PM||||To follow up on this thought:<P>"Speaking of that, is anything loose in there???<P>Drive it up on ramps and see if the radiator mount is solid, or if you can wiggle anything else..."<P>Check the topside, too. The jack is over the passenger wheel. If the screw has loosened, then that would make a crashing sound. Make sure the decklid brace is solidly mounted to the car and the lid.<P>I once had a similar thing. A bad shock made a noise over bumps, but it was more of a thump sound.||||reg||3
Z||000006||85 gt fiero||09-25-2001||10:57 PM||||Maybe your engines knocking......HeHeHeHe||||reg||12
Z||000007||Mach10||09-26-2001||12:50 AM||||Here's one that I'm having:<P>see if it bangs/rattles with the brakes on. I've managed to lose both rattle clips on my pads, and they make a HELl of a racket. Seems to be It, though...<BR>||||reg||7
